.TH XYMON-THEME 1 "2026-08-22" "Version 4.3.30" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
xymon-theme \- select a Xymon web theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymon-theme list"
.br
.B "xymon-theme current"
.br
.B "xymon-theme activate"
.I THEME
.br
.B "xymon-theme disable"

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBxymon-theme\fR selects an installed Xymon web theme without modifying
xymonserver.cfg, xymonmenu.cfg, stock web assets, or stock templates.
Activation writes the presentation settings from the selected package to
xymonserver.d/90-theme.cfg using an atomic rename. The command manages only
that drop-in and refuses to replace or remove it when it lacks the
xymon-theme ownership marker.

The built-in classic-blue theme is the default and uses Xymon's existing
blue menu. No drop-in is needed for this default. The built-in classic-grey
theme selects the existing grey menu. Disabling a selected theme removes the
managed drop-in and returns to classic-blue.

A theme package has a theme.conf manifest and may have static assets and
templates. The manifest may set only XYMONSKIN, XYMONMENUSKIN,
XYMONBODYCSS, XYMONBODYMENUCSS, XYMONBODYHEADER, XYMONBODYFOOTER, and
XYMONLOGO. Monitoring and runtime settings are rejected.

.SH COMMANDS
.IP "\fBlist\fR"
Print the identifiers of installed theme packages, one per line.
.IP "\fBcurrent\fR"
Print the active theme identifier. This prints "classic-blue" when no
managed selection exists.
.IP "\fBactivate\fR \fITHEME\fR"
Validate and activate THEME. Theme identifiers begin with an ASCII letter
or digit and contain only letters, digits, dots, underscores, and hyphens.
.IP "\fBdisable\fR"
Remove the managed selection and restore the default classic-blue theme.

.SH FILES
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/etc/themes/\fITHEME\fB/theme.conf\fR"
Installed presentation settings for THEME.
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/etc/xymonserver.d/90-theme.cfg\fR"
The active selection generated and owned by xymon-theme.
.IP "\fB$XYMONSERVERWWWURL/menu/themes/\fITHEME\fB/\fR"
URL namespace for a theme's installed static assets.
.IP "\fB$XYMONHOME/web/themes/\fITHEME\fB/\fR"
Optional theme-specific templates. Packages use unique names here and do
not replace stock templates.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymonserver.cfg(5)
